{
  "sourceLanguage" : "en",
  "strings" : {
    "\"%@\" is not a number." : {
      "comment" : "Message when the text typed in Go to Percent is no number. %@ is what the user typed, shown in quotation marks.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "“%@” no es un número."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "« %@ » n’est pas un nombre."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "“%@” non è un numero."
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "“%@” não é um número."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "\"%@\" plays the next book in the same folder by sort order." : {
      "comment" : "Explanation under the When book ends pop-up in the Playback settings. %@ is the title of the pop-up's choice that plays the next book, as the pop-up shows it.",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "„%@“ gibt das nächste Buch im selben Ordner nach der Sortierreihenfolge wieder."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "«%@» reproduce el siguiente libro de la misma carpeta, en orden de clasificación."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "« %@ » lit le livre suivant du même dossier, selon l’ordre de tri."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "“%@” riproduce il libro successivo nella stessa cartella, in base all’ordinamento."
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "“%@” reproduz o próximo livro da mesma pasta, na ordem de classificação."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@ %@" : {
      "comment" : "A row button's name with the row's subject, so VoiceOver tells one row's button from the next, such as \"Delete Marker 3\". %1$@ is the button's name and %2$@ the row's subject.\nAnnouncement of the microphone level every few seconds while recording. %1$@ is the level's label and %2$@ is the level in words, such as \"minus 12 decibels, good\".\nJoins two whole sentences into one text. %1$@ is the first sentence and %2$@ the second. English puts a space between them; Japanese and Chinese join sentences with no space at all, so change only the separator.",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "%1$@ %2$@"
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "%1$@ %2$@"
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "%1$@ %2$@"
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "%1$@ %2$@"
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "%1$@ %2$@"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "%1$@ %2$@"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@ %@, which TextMouth can't export with its structure." : {
      "comment" : "The first sentence of the alert an export shows when a chapter nests too deeply. %1$@ names what nests, such as \"Chapter 2 of Deep Notes\", and %2$@ is the clause that says how deep, such as \"nests quotes, lists, or emphasis more than 128 levels deep\".",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "%1$@ %2$@, und TextMouth kann das nicht mit seiner Struktur exportieren."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "%1$@ %2$@, which TextMouth can't export with its structure."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "%1$@ %2$@, y TextMouth no puede exportarlo con su estructura."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "%1$@ %2$@, ce que TextMouth ne peut pas exporter avec sa structure."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "%1$@ %2$@, e TextMouth non può esportarne la struttura."
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "%1$@ %2$@, e o TextMouth não consegue exportar com essa estrutura."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@ %@." : {
      "comment" : "Says why a book's download cannot be deleted or replaced now. The first %@ is the book's title in quotation marks, or \"It\"; the second is a clause such as \"is open in a reader\" or \"is being transcribed, and deleting its download now would lose the transcript\".",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "%1$@ %2$@."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "%1$@ %2$@."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "%1$@ %2$@."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "%1$@ %2$@."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "%1$@ %2$@."
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "%1$@ %2$@."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@ %lld of %lld" : {
      "comment" : "A question's title followed by its place among the questions waiting, when the title ends in a question mark. %1$@ is the title, %2$lld the question's place and %3$lld the number of questions, such as \"Create Folder for Imported Books? 2 of 3\".",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "%1$@ %2$lld von %3$lld"
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "%1$@ %2$lld of %3$lld"
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "%1$@ %2$lld de %3$lld"
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "%1$@ %2$lld sur %3$lld"
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "%1$@ %2$lld di %3$lld"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "%1$@ %2$lld de %3$lld"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@ (%@)" : {
      "comment" : "A feed that could not be subscribed to, with the reason in parentheses. The first %@ is the feed's title; the second is the reason, in the engine's words.\nOne group of a PDF's pages that text recognition (OCR) could not run on, with the reason. %1$@ is the pages, such as \"pages 3 and 7\", and %2$@ the reason, a phrase in English.\nThe second choice of the Log location pop-up in the Storage settings. %1$@ is the choice's name, and %2$@ is the folder's name on this Mac, a path that stays as written, such as ~/Library/Logs/TextMouth.",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "%1$@ (%2$@)"
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "%1$@ (%2$@)"
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "%1$@ (%2$@)"
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "%1$@ (%2$@)"
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "%1$@ (%2$@)"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "%1$@ (%2$@)"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@ (current heading) - level %lld" : {
      "comment" : "What VoiceOver says for the heading being read, in the headings list. %1$@ is the heading's text; %2$lld is its level, 1 for the biggest heading.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "%1$@ (current heading) - level %2$lld"
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "%1$@ (encabezado actual) - nivel %2$lld"
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "%@ (en-tête actuel), niveau %lld"
          }
        },
        "it" : {
