    "“%@” can't be read as %@: %@ Nothing was changed." : {
      "comment" : "Text of Speak Info, Book Information's braille code and text encoding rows, and the re-read alerts. Why the book titled bookTitle was not read again with the braille file characters named codeName: its file is not braille in them, as reason, the reader's own sentence (BrailleFileError), says, and nothing changed. It has the shape of an encoding's refusal (TextEncodingWording.notValidRefusal(bookTitle:encoding:)): \"“Ledger” can't be read as Eurobraille, six-dot (German-speaking countries): Line 3 holds the control character U+0007, which is not Eurobraille. Nothing was changed.\". Placeholders in order: bookTitle, codeName, reason.",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "„%1$@“ kann nicht als %2$@ gelesen werden: %3$@ Nichts wurde geändert."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "“%1$@” can't be read as %2$@: %3$@ Nothing was changed."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "“%1$@” no se puede leer como %2$@: %3$@ No se cambió nada."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "« %@ » ne peut pas être lu en %@ : %@ Rien n’a été modifié."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "«%@» non può essere letto come %@: %@ Nulla è stato modificato."
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "“%1$@” não pode ser lido como %2$@: %3$@ Nada foi alterado."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "“%@” changed while it was being replaced, so TextMouth left both copies as they are. Choose Replace Existing again." : {
      "comment" : "What the duplicate question says when the library's copy changed while the new copy was being made ready. %@ is the book's title. \"Replace Existing\" is a button of the question.",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "„%@“ hat sich beim Ersetzen geändert, daher hat TextMouth beide Kopien unverändert gelassen. Wähle „Vorhandenes ersetzen“ erneut."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "“%@” cambió mientras se reemplazaba, así que TextMouth dejó ambas copias como están. Elige Reemplazar el existente de nuevo."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "« %@ » a changé pendant son remplacement, donc TextMouth a laissé les deux copies telles quelles. Choisissez de nouveau Remplacer l’existant."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "«%@» è cambiato durante la sostituzione, quindi TextMouth ha lasciato entrambe le copie come sono. Scegli di nuovo Sostituisci l’esistente."
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "“%@” mudou enquanto era substituído, então o TextMouth deixou as duas cópias como estão. Escolha Substituir o existente novamente."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "“%@” could not be moved back after a failed move, so its files are at %@ instead of %@: %@" : {
      "comment" : "Failure notice: a book's files could not be put back after a move failed. %1$@ is the book's title; %2$@ is where its files are now; %3$@ is where they belong; %4$@ is the reason, a sentence from the system.",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "„%1$@“ konnte nach einem fehlgeschlagenen Verschieben nicht zurückverschoben werden, daher liegen seine Dateien in %2$@ statt in %3$@: %4$@"
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "“%1$@” could not be moved back after a failed move, so its files are at %2$@ instead of %3$@: %4$@"
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "No se pudo devolver «%1$@» a su sitio tras un traslado fallido, así que sus archivos están en %2$@ en lugar de %3$@: %4$@"
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "« %1$@ » n’a pas pu être remis à sa place après l’échec d’un déplacement ; ses fichiers sont dans %2$@ au lieu de %3$@ : %4$@"
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Non è stato possibile rimettere a posto “%@” dopo uno spostamento non riuscito, quindi i suoi file sono in %@ invece che in %@: %@"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "“%1$@” não pôde ser movido de volta após uma movimentação com falha, então os arquivos dele estão em %2$@ em vez de %3$@: %4$@"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "“%@” couldn't be downloaded from iCloud. Check the connection, then add it again." : {
      "comment" : "What VoiceOver says when a file's download from iCloud stalled and the import was cancelled. %@ is the file's name.",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "„%@“ konnte nicht aus iCloud heruntergeladen werden. Prüfe die Verbindung und füge die Datei dann erneut hinzu."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "No se pudo descargar «%@» desde iCloud. Comprueba la conexión y vuelve a agregarlo."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "« %@ » n’a pas pu être téléchargé depuis iCloud. Vérifiez la connexion, puis ajoutez-le de nouveau."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Impossibile scaricare “%@” da iCloud. Controlla la connessione, poi aggiungilo di nuovo."
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Não foi possível baixar “%@” do iCloud. Verifique a conexão e adicione-o de novo."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "“%@” couldn't be read: %@." : {
      "comment" : "Error shown when an audio file cannot be read. %1$@ is the audio file's name; %2$@ is the reason, a short phrase in English.",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "„%1$@“ konnte nicht gelesen werden: %2$@."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "“%1$@” couldn't be read: %2$@."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "No se pudo leer “%1$@”: %2$@."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "« %1$@ » n’a pas pu être lu : %2$@."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Impossibile leggere “%1$@”: %2$@."
          }
        },
